TASK: Improve image selection and attachment behavior in the BlueMind chat composer.

This task has TWO specific changes:

1. Number selected images in the media picker.
2. Show selected images INSIDE the chat composer/input, not outside it.

Do not redesign unrelated chat UI.
Do not change backend message logic unless required to preserve attachment order.

==================================================
1. MULTI-IMAGE SELECTION WITH ORDER NUMBERS
==================================================

When the user taps recent photos inside the + media sheet:

Allow selecting multiple images.

Each selected image must display its selection ORDER as a number.

Example:

First selected image:
1

Second selected image:
2

Third selected image:
3

and so on.

The selection badge should appear in the top-right corner of each thumbnail.

Requirements:
- use a circular iOS-style selection badge
- Blue/iOS accent is fine for the selected badge
- white number inside
- unselected image shows normal empty selection circle if appropriate
- preserve the exact order in which the user selected the images

If the user deselects one image:
recalculate the order correctly.

Example:
Selected:
1, 2, 3

User deselects image 2.

Remaining selected images should become:
1, 2

Do not leave:
1, 3

==================================================
2. CONFIRM SELECTION
==================================================

Do not immediately close the media sheet after every photo tap.

Allow the user to select multiple photos first.

Then provide a clear confirmation control:

✓

or an iOS-style Done action.

When user confirms:
- close the media sheet
- attach all selected images to the current chat
- preserve selection order

If user cancels/closes without confirming:
do not attach unintended images.

==================================================
3. SELECTED IMAGES MUST APPEAR INSIDE THE COMPOSER
==================================================

Current/undesired behavior:
attachments appear outside or above the composer as a separate floating section.

Change this.

Selected image attachments must become part of the SAME composer container.

The composer should expand vertically to contain them.

Conceptually:

┌──────────────────────────────────┐
│ [img 1] [img 2] [img 3]         │
│                                  │
│ Ask anything...                  │
│                                  │
│ [+]                         [mic][↑]
└──────────────────────────────────┘

The images belong INSIDE the rounded/glass composer.

Do not place the attachment row outside the input.

==================================================
4. COMPOSER EXPANSION
==================================================

When no images are attached:
composer uses normal compact height.

When one or more images are attached:
composer expands upward automatically.

Inside the composer:

TOP:
attachment preview row

BOTTOM:
text input + controls

The composer should remain one unified BlueMind iOS glass component.

Do not create a separate card above it.

==================================================
5. IMAGE PREVIEWS
==================================================

Image previews should:

- use compact thumbnails
- rounded corners
- preserve aspect ratio/crop cleanly
- have consistent spacing
- support horizontal scrolling if many images are attached
- remain fully inside composer bounds

Each attachment preview should have a small remove X.

Tapping X:
- removes that specific attachment
- does not clear the others
- composer resizes naturally

==================================================
6. ORDER
==================================================

The attachment preview row must preserve selection order.

If selected:
photo A = 1
photo B = 2
photo C = 3

Composer preview order must be:

A, B, C

Do not reorder by filename, timestamp, or photo-library position after confirmation.

==================================================
7. TEXT + IMAGES
==================================================

User must be able to:

- select images
- return to composer
- type text with the images still attached
- send text + images together

Example:

[image 1] [image 2]

"Explain the difference between these two designs."

Send:
one message request containing both the text and ordered attachments.

==================================================
8. KEYBOARD
==================================================

When composer contains images and keyboard opens:

- composer stays directly above keyboard
- attachments remain inside composer
- composer can grow but must not cover the whole screen
- message area above remains scrollable
- no overlap
- no duplicate composer

If necessary, limit attachment preview row height and use horizontal scrolling.

==================================================
9. IOS / GLASS STYLE
==================================================

Preserve the current BlueMind iOS / Liquid Glass composer design.

The expanded composer must still use:

- same translucent glass
- same border
- same radius
- same + button
- same microphone
- same send button

Do not turn the expanded composer into a flat gray rectangle.

==================================================
10. CAMERA / FILES
==================================================

This attachment-inside-composer behavior should also support future/current Camera and Files attachments where appropriate.

For this task, ensure Photos work correctly first.

Do not break Camera or Files.

==================================================
11. DO NOT TOUCH
==================================================

Do not change:

- normal message styling
- AI mode selector
- header
- backend AI behavior
- Projects
- Search
- Writing Mode layout
- unrelated screens

Only change:
- photo multi-select UX
- selection numbering
- confirmation
- attachment preview placement inside composer

